WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.253
Week 28: Subjunctive: Doubt, Purpose, and Contingency. qualify certainty state purpose and conditions plan for contingencies

2
00:00:09.253 --> 00:00:16.223
Cultural lens. Evidence, rumor, and calibrated claims in media and professional discussion.

3
00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:28.401
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:28.401 --> 00:00:40.429
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:49.450
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:49.450 --> 00:01:17.116
Model language. Dudo que la cifra sea correcta. — I doubt that the figure is correct. Es probable que llueva esta noche. — It will probably rain tonight. Salimos temprano para que haya tiempo suficiente. — We are leaving early so that there is enough time. No firmaremos a menos que cambien la cláusula. — We will not sign unless they change the clause. Llámame en cuanto llegues. — Call me as soon as you arrive.

7
00:01:17.116 --> 00:01:27.121
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
